                    </h2>
                    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-sm">
                        <div class="rounded-lg border border-stone bg-boxwood-pale p-4"><p class="font-bold text-charcoal mb-1">1. Declare</p><p class="text-charcoal-mid">List the page names once in `vars.pages`.</p></div>
                        <div class="rounded-lg border border-stone bg-white p-4"><p class="font-bold text-charcoal mb-1">2. Expand</p><p class="text-charcoal-mid">`foreach` creates one `page` target per entry.</p></div>
                        <div class="rounded-lg border border-stone bg-white p-4"><p class="font-bold text-charcoal mb-1">3. Render</p><p class="text-charcoal-mid">Invoke Pandoc for each Markdown page.</p></div>
                        <div class="rounded-lg border border-stone bg-boxwood-pale p-4"><p class="font-bold text-charcoal mb-1">4. Assemble</p><p class="text-charcoal-mid">Build `site/index.html` from the source pages with `pandoc --standalone`.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </div>

